{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('../exit-interview.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text())\nd['sourceInformation']['testing']='149 automated checks passed with zero failures: headless Chromium software WebGPU; complete route with normal hazards and physics; native animation, collision, checkpoints, collectibles, saves, emulated standard gamepad, real multitouch events, offline PCM and live audio, direct two-page co-op, and all four official AI Hub harness scenarios. 1920×1080 WebGL2 captures support visual review. Physical controllers, real phones, audible mix quality and internet NAT traversal: unknown.'\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n '8 issues were found: 7 implementation defects and software-GPU context exhaustion in a long browser run. All were addressed. The final full suite passed 149 checks with zero failures.',\n '2 blocked normal route progress: a thick floating ledge obstructed an early landing, and the swimming region ended before the river exit. Both were corrected.',\n 'The complete scripted playthrough with normal hazards and physics, from the first gap through both rescues, ladders, balloon, lunchbox, return trolley and camp bell.',\n 'Headless WebGPU screenshots were blank on this machine. They could not validate the art, so state checks and WebGL2 fallback captures were used instead.'\n]\nd['engineFeedback']=[\n 'Three.js native toon materials, its scene graph and AnimationMixer made the procedural inked caverns and expressive explorers straightforward.',\n 'Yes. I initially gave floating ledges full terrain thickness and ended the swim region too early. Co-op testing also exposed short input pulses being overwritten before host simulation.',\n 'The exploration rules, controller-first menu focus, buoyant swimming, balloon riding, retained discoveries and authoritative shared-world co-op.',\n 'Coordinating fixed-step Rapier physics, AnimationMixer visuals and network snapshots, including a host with no player. Repeated headless pages also needed careful GPU cleanup and isolated test phases.',\n 'none',\n 'A first-party controller action and UI focus layer would reduce the amount of game-specific input plumbing.'\n]\nd['promptFeedback']=[\n 'The source-inspired vertical slice, controller-first presentation, live balance tools and required attract mode gave the game a clear identity.',\n 'Whether the ban on internet research also covered the required live hub contract. I treated the supplied protocol and dependency downloads as implementation access and performed no internet searches.',\n 'Completing the exploration loop and both multiplayer paths in one self-contained file, including the server-only host, input edge handling and final shared return trip.',\n 'Include the required hub integration files in the task context, or explicitly distinguish reading that contract from internet research.'\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nissues=[\n {'id':1,'kind':'inspection','critical':False,'issue':'A getter and a test control shared the input property name and prevented test-mode boot.','fix':'Separated the input device getter and test input method.'},\n {'id':2,'kind':'gameplay','critical':True,'issue':'A full-thickness floating ledge obstructed the first gap landing.','fix':'Authored thin optional platforms with clear walk-under space.'},\n {'id':3,'kind':'gameplay','critical':True,'issue':'The swim region stopped short of the riverbank exit.','fix':'Extended buoyancy through the shoreline handoff.'},\n {'id':4,'kind':'inspection','critical':False,'issue':'Object.assign froze an animation-state getter in the test API.','fix':'Defined a live inspection getter.'},\n {'id':5,'kind':'accessibility','critical':False,'issue':'The focused menu arrow changed accessible button names, breaking exact-name selection.','fix':'Added stable explicit accessible labels.'},\n {'id':6,'kind':'network','critical':False,'issue':'A departed direct peer could leave a stale connected seat.','fix':'Added departure signaling, connection-state recovery and a heartbeat timeout.'},\n {'id':7,'kind':'network','critical':False,'issue':'Remote interact and jump pulses could be overwritten by a later packet before host simulation.','fix':'Latched discrete commands until the host consumes them.'},\n {'id':8,'kind':'test environment','critical':False,'issue':'A long multi-context software-GPU test run exhausted rendering contexts.','fix':'Disposed rendering resources on page exit and isolated heavy test phases in fresh browsers.'}\n]\nPath('test-artifacts/issue-history.json').write_text(json.dumps(issues,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nprint('Exit interview JSON parsed; 15 source fields, 14 feedback answers, and catalogue metadata complete.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('../exit-interview.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text())\nd['sourceInformation']['testing']='149 automated checks passed with zero failures: headless Chromium software WebGPU; complete route with normal hazards and physics; native animation, collision, checkpoints, collectibles, saves, emulated standard gamepad, real multitouch events, offline PCM and live audio, direct two-page co-op, and all four official AI Hub harness scenarios. 1920×1080 WebGL2 captures support visual review. Physical controllers, real phones, audible mix quality and internet NAT traversal: unknown.'\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n '8 issues were found: 7 implementation defects and software-GPU context exhaustion in a long browser run. All were addressed. The final full suite passed 149 checks with zero failures.',\n '2 blocked normal route progress: a thick floating ledge obstructed an early landing, and the swimming region ended before the river exit. Both were corrected.',\n 'The complete scripted playthrough with normal hazards and physics, from the first gap through both rescues, ladders, balloon, lunchbox, return trolley and camp bell.',\n 'Headless WebGPU screenshots were blank on this machine. They could not validate the art, so state checks and WebGL2 fallback captures were used instead.'\n]\nd['engineFeedback']=[\n 'Three.js native toon materials, its scene graph and AnimationMixer made the procedural inked caverns and expressive explorers straightforward.',\n 'Yes. I initially gave floating ledges full terrain thickness and ended the swim region too early. Co-op testing also exposed short input pulses being overwritten before host simulation.',\n 'The exploration rules, controller-first menu focus, buoyant swimming, balloon riding, retained discoveries and authoritative shared-world co-op.',\n 'Coordinating fixed-step Rapier physics, AnimationMixer visuals and network snapshots, including a host with no player. Repeated headless pages also needed careful GPU cleanup and isolated test phases.',\n 'none',\n 'A first-party controller action and UI focus layer would reduce the amount of game-specific input plumbing.'\n]\nd['promptFeedback']=[\n 'The source-inspired vertical slice, controller-first presentation, live balance tools and required attract mode gave the game a clear identity.',\n 'Whether the ban on internet research also covered the required live hub contract. I treated the supplied protocol and dependency downloads as implementation access and performed no internet searches.',\n 'Completing the exploration loop and both multiplayer paths in one self-contained file, including the server-only host, input edge handling and final shared return trip.',\n 'Include the required hub integration files in the task context, or explicitly distinguish reading that contract from internet research.'\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nissues=[\n {'id':1,'kind':'inspection','critical':False,'issue':'A getter and a test control shared the input property name and prevented test-mode boot.','fix':'Separated the input device getter and test input method.'},\n {'id':2,'kind':'gameplay','critical':True,'issue':'A full-thickness floating ledge obstructed the first gap landing.','fix':'Authored thin optional platforms with clear walk-under space.'},\n {'id':3,'kind':'gameplay','critical':True,'issue':'The swim region stopped short of the riverbank exit.','fix':'Extended buoyancy through the shoreline handoff.'},\n {'id':4,'kind':'inspection','critical':False,'issue':'Object.assign froze an animation-state getter in the test API.','fix':'Defined a live inspection getter.'},\n {'id':5,'kind':'accessibility','critical':False,'issue':'The focused menu arrow changed accessible button names, breaking exact-name selection.','fix':'Added stable explicit accessible labels.'},\n {'id':6,'kind':'network','critical':False,'issue':'A departed direct peer could leave a stale connected seat.','fix':'Added departure signaling, connection-state recovery and a heartbeat timeout.'},\n {'id':7,'kind':'network','critical':False,'issue':'Remote interact and jump pulses could be overwritten by a later packet before host simulation.','fix':'Latched discrete commands until the host consumes them.'},\n {'id':8,'kind':'test environment','critical':False,'issue':'A long multi-context software-GPU test run exhausted rendering contexts.','fix':'Disposed rendering resources on page exit and isolated heavy test phases in fresh browsers.'}\n]\nPath('test-artifacts/issue-history.json').write_text(json.dumps(issues,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nprint('Exit interview JSON parsed; 15 source fields, 14 feedback answers, and catalogue metadata complete.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Exit interview JSON parsed; 15 source fields, 14 feedback answers, and catalogue metadata complete.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
